    "hairscripts_faq_split_MWpNL3": {
      "type": "hairscripts-faq-split",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_aYjpAY": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Will this work on my hair type or texture?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. HairScripts™ works on all hair types, textures, and patterns — straight, wavy, curly, coily, fine, or thick. The science behind hair growth is the same for everyone. Your follicles need the same nutrients, the same circulation, the same hormonal balance, and the same protection from oxidative stress regardless of what your strands look like above the scalp.<br/><br/>This formula was built to support the root cause of thinning, not the strand itself. That means it works underneath your texture — supporting follicle health from the inside out.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_hBGTxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "I'm on Ozempic, Wegovy, or another GLP-1 medication. Will this work for me?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — and you may actually need this more than most. GLP-1 medications significantly reduce appetite, which often means a significant drop in protein, iron, zinc, and Vitamin D intake. Combined with the metabolic stress of rapid weight loss, this triggers a delayed shedding pattern that shows up 2–4 months in.<br/><br/>HairScripts™ was formulated to address exactly this kind of nutritional gap. Bioavailable iron, zinc, Vitamin D, collagen, and pea protein directly replace what GLP-1 users tend to lose. Ashwagandha supports the cortisol response to major metabolic shifts.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_iNbfbe": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "I'm postpartum or breastfeeding — can I take this?",
            "answer": "<p>Postpartum yes, breastfeeding requires a conversation with your provider. The formula was designed with postpartum recovery in mind — it addresses the iron depletion, hormonal crash, and stress-related shedding that typically appear 3–6 months after delivery.<br/><br/>If you're currently breastfeeding, please review the ingredients with your healthcare provider before starting. While the ingredients are generally well-tolerated, your individual situation should be evaluated by someone who knows your medical history.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_B3Vw9i": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "I'm in perimenopause or menopause. Will this work for me?",
            "answer": "<p>This is one of the patterns the formula was specifically built around. As estrogen declines, your follicles become more sensitive to androgen activity. At the same time, cortisol regulation shifts, antioxidant defense drops, and the protective hormonal environment that kept your follicles in the growth phase starts to disappear.<br/><br/>HairScripts™ supports healthy DHT activity, cortisol balance, scalp circulation, and the antioxidant layer your body loses access to during this transition. All in one daily formula.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Hchjtn": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Will this work if I have PCOS, insulin resistance, or thyroid issues?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes for most situations, with one important nuance worth being transparent about. PCOS and insulin resistance raise androgen activity at the follicle, and thyroid dysfunction slows follicle cell division — these root causes need to be addressed at the source, not at the strand. HairScripts™ supports insulin sensitivity, healthy DHT activity, and the selenium and zinc pathways that support thyroid-related follicle function.<br/><br/>The transparency piece: HairScripts™ contains Ashwagandha, which has clinical research supporting subclinical and underactive thyroid function (hypothyroidism, Hashimoto's). However, women with hyperthyroidism or Graves' disease should speak with their provider before starting — Ashwagandha can increase thyroid hormone production, which is helpful when your thyroid is underactive and a concern when it's overactive. The same conversation applies if you're currently on thyroid replacement medication like levothyroxine.<br/><br/>This isn't a brand-wide contraindication. It's a ‘talk to your provider first’ conversation for one specific subset of thyroid patients. Please continue any prescribed medications — HairScripts™ is designed to work alongside them, not replace them.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_6KNWc7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Can I take this with other supplements or prescription medications?",
            "answer": "<p>HairScripts™ is generally compatible with most supplements and medications. However, since the formula contains iron, zinc, and clinically-active ingredients like Saw Palmetto and Ashwagandha, please review the ingredient list with your healthcare provider if you are on prescription medications — especially blood thinners, hormone therapies, thyroid medications, sedatives, immunosuppressants, or antidepressants.<br/><br/>If you're already taking a separate iron or multivitamin, you may not need it anymore once you start HairScripts™. Check with your provider to avoid stacking.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_T3TfGm": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "I've tried everything — Nutrafol, Viviscal, biotin, oils, serums. Why would this be different?",
            "answer": "<p>Because most of what you tried was built around one pathway. Biotin focuses on a single vitamin. Most leading brands focus on one or two pathways. Meanwhile your hair loss is probably being driven by 3–5 root causes simultaneously — stress, hormones, nutrient depletion, inflammation, and circulation.<br/><br/>HairScripts™ was built differently. It addresses all 9 root causes of hormonal hair loss in one formula — so you're covered at every level, even if you haven't identified the specific trigger yet. The formula didn't fail you before. The formulas you tried were built for one problem and you have nine.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_f9Gmmf": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Can men use this too?",
            "answer": "<p>The formula was specifically developed for women navigating hormonal hair loss — the patterns that show up during postpartum, perimenopause, stress, and metabolic shifts. While men can technically take it, the dosing and ingredient profile were calibrated around female hormonal biology.<br/><br/>For men experiencing hair loss, the underlying drivers are typically different and may require a different formulation strategy. We don't currently have a men's formula, but it may be on the horizon.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_VNqzEc": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Is this for all hair types and textures?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — HairScripts works on all hair types, textures, and patterns. Hair biology is universal. If your follicles are weakened, this formula supports regrowth at the root level.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_BCBBnr": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "What makes HairScripts™ different from Nutrafol or Viviscal?",
            "answer": "<p>Three things. First, HairScripts™ addresses all 9 root causes of hormonal hair loss simultaneously — not one pathway at a time. Second, every ingredient is clinically dosed at levels research actually supports — not micro-dosed for marketing. Third, this formula was developed by a pharmaceutical industry expert who personally lost nearly 60% of her hair and had the clinical training to understand exactly why.<br/><br/>That combination — multi-pathway formulation, clinical dosing, and pharmaceutical-grade development — is the entire difference.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_VkfP8N": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "Is this just another biotin pill?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Biotin alone fails for most women because hair growth requires far more than one vitamin. Your follicles rely on iron, zinc, Vitamin D, selenium, copper, and absorption cofactors working together — alongside hormonal balance, cortisol regulation, scalp circulation, and antioxidant defense.<br/><br/>HairScripts™ was built as a coordinated system, not a single-ingredient shortcut. Biotin alone is like trying to build a house with only one tool.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Qi3MJ7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "I've read concerns about Ashwagandha. Is it safe in this formula?",
            "answer": "<p>This is exactly the kind of question I want you to ask. Ashwagandha is one of the most clinically studied adaptogens in modern science — with over 3,000 years of traditional use and dozens of peer-reviewed studies on cortisol reduction, stress-related shedding, and follicle recovery. The research is robust.<br/><br/>That said, transparency matters. Ashwagandha is not the right fit for everyone. Women with hyperthyroidism or Graves' disease should avoid it. Women on thyroid replacement medication should speak with their provider first. Women who are pregnant should also consult their healthcare provider before starting.<br/><br/>For everyone else — and especially for women navigating stress-related shedding, postpartum recovery, perimenopause, and burnout — Ashwagandha is one of the most powerful tools in the formula. At 350mg, HairScripts™ delivers a clinically-effective dose using KSM-66®, the most studied standardized extract on the market.<br/><br/>If you have any underlying condition or you're on prescription medications, please review the full ingredient list with your healthcare provider before starting. That goes for every supplement, not just this one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_3CtYRi": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "Why does HairScripts™ require 4 capsules per day?",
            "answer": "<p>Because clinical dosing requires it. To deliver Ashwagandha at 350mg, Saw Palmetto at 320mg, Hydrolyzed Collagen at 300mg, L-Citrulline at 250mg, and the full spectrum of supporting nutrients at levels that research actually supports — 4 capsules is what fits the volume.</p><p>Single-capsule formulas exist, but they exist by under-dosing every ingredient. We chose to dose at clinical levels instead. Take all 4 daily, with or without food, for best results.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_cpeKzP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "Is this drug-free? Does it contain minoxidil?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, it's drug-free. No, it does not contain minoxidil — or any prescription pharmaceutical. HairScripts™ is a science-backed dietary supplement formulated with clinically-studied vitamins, minerals, botanical extracts, and amino acids.</p><p>Minoxidil works for some women, but it requires lifelong topical application, can cause rebound shedding when stopped, and only addresses one pathway. HairScripts™ is the alternative — a multi-pathway system that supports your follicles from the inside without prescription side effects.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_nQVh7C": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "Is HairScripts™ third-party tested?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. HairScripts™ is manufactured in a GMP-certified facility and undergoes third-party testing for purity, potency, and contaminant screening. The formula was reviewed and approved by a licensed healthcare provider before launch.</p><p>You deserve to know exactly what's going into your body — and that the dose on the label matches what's actually in the capsule. We take that responsibility seriously.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_86rwCb": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "Where is HairScripts™ manufactured?",
            "answer": "<p>HairScripts™ is manufactured in the United States in a GMP-certified facility. Every batch is tested for purity, potency, and contaminants before shipping.</p><p>Manufacturing transparency matters in the supplement industry — and we believe you should be able to trust that what's on the label is what's in the bottle.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_9ibBAW": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "What's in HairScripts™? Is the formula transparent?",
            "answer": "<p>Every ingredient is listed on the label with its specific clinical dose — no proprietary blends, no hidden actives, no marketing-only ingredients. The core formula includes Ashwagandha KSM-66 at 350mg, Saw Palmetto at 320mg, Hydrolyzed Collagen at 300mg, L-Citrulline at 250mg, MSM at 150mg, Beta-Sitosterol at 120mg, Alpha-Lipoic Acid at 100mg, CoQ10 at 80mg, plus Vitamin D, Niacin, Ferrochel® iron, Albion® zinc, Selenium, Copper, and additional supporting nutrients.</p><p>Full transparency is a non-negotiable brand standard. You can see every ingredient and dose on the product page.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_R4WqzN": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "How soon will I see results?",
            "answer": "<p>Most women notice less shedding within 4–8 weeks, and visible density improvements between 90 days and 6 months. Hair grows in months, not days — that's not a marketing limitation, that's how the growth cycle actually works. It takes at least 90 days to biohack your body from a cellular level.<br/><br/>Consistency is the variable that determines your timeline. Take 4 capsules daily without skipping. Most women who quit at week 6 quit right before the results would have started showing up. Don't be one of them.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_iKeBzF": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "Will this make me shed more before it gets better?",
            "answer": "<p>Some women experience a brief uptick in shedding within the first 2–4 weeks — this is called a transition shed. It happens when dormant follicles are pushed back into the active growth phase and release the resting strand they were holding onto. New, stronger strands grow underneath.<br/><br/>It feels scary in the moment, but it's actually a sign the formula is working. If you experience it, do not stop. Push through and you'll see the regrowth within the next 30–60 days.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_jQKcpK": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "What if I don't see results in 90 days?",
            "answer": "<p>90 days is when results begin to become visible. Full results compound between 4–6 months as your follicles complete additional growth cycles. If you've been consistent and you're not seeing the results you expected, the most common reasons are: an underlying root cause that needs medical evaluation (often thyroid or ferritin), or an inconsistent daily dose.<br/><br/>Individual results vary based on age, genetics, health, stress, and consistency. HairScripts™ does not guarantee specific results, timelines, or outcomes. For complete details, please see our Terms & Conditions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_RdUHCz": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "What happens if I stop taking HairScripts™?",
            "answer": "<p>Hair growth is an ongoing biological process. Your follicles need consistent nutritional and hormonal support to maintain results. If you stop taking HairScripts™, the underlying drivers — cortisol, DHT activity, nutrient depletion, oxidative stress — will return to their pre-supplement levels. Over time, your hair may revert.<br/><br/>This isn't a 30-day cleanse. It's a long-term wellness commitment. Most women who see significant results choose to stay on the formula at a maintenance level.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_nXeKGy": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "What if I've had thinning for years — is it too late?",
            "answer": "<p>It's almost never too late. Follicles that have been miniaturized are still alive — they're being biochemically suppressed. As long as the follicle hasn't completely scarred over, intervention works. The key variable is consistency over time.<br/><br/>Women with long-standing thinning often need more time to see results — 6 months minimum, sometimes 12 months for full transformation. The follicles need extra time to reverse years of cumulative damage. But the recovery is real, and it compounds.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_GcfXKD": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "How will I know it's working?",
            "answer": "<p>The signs in order: less shedding in the shower and on your brush (weeks 4–8), scalp feels healthier and less reactive (weeks 6–12), visible baby hairs at the hairline and part (months 3–4), and noticeable density and fullness (months 4–6).<br/><br/>Take a photo of your part, edges, and crown the day you start — same lighting, same angle. Compare every 30 days. The day-to-day changes are too small to see in the mirror, but the month-to-month progress is undeniable when you have the photos to compare.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_X7QgJj": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": " Are there any side effects?",
            "answer": "<p>HairScripts™ is formulated with clinically-studied ingredients that are generally well-tolerated. Some women report mild stomach sensitivity when taking the capsules on a completely empty stomach — if this happens, take with food. A small percentage of women may experience initial fatigue or temporary digestive changes during the first 1–2 weeks as their body adjusts to the iron and adaptogenic ingredients.<br/><br/>If you experience anything unusual or have concerns about an existing health condition, please discontinue use and consult your healthcare provider.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_BVCw9J": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "How does the subscription work?",
            "answer": "<p>Choose your supply (Monthly, Quarterly, or Semi-Annual), and HairScripts™ ships to your door automatically at the frequency you selected (every 30, 90, or 180 days). Your payment method on file is charged automatically on each renewal date.<br/><br/>By signing up for a subscription, you authorize recurring charges at the interval you chose until you cancel. You can manage everything from your customer portal at hairscriptsbybevy.com. For complete subscription terms, please see our Subscription Management policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_qyjdbz": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "Can I cancel or pause my subscription anytime?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. You can cancel or pause your subscription at any time through your customer portal at hairscriptsbybevy.com, or by emailing support@hairscriptsbybevy.com.<br/><br/>Important: cancellations must be received before your next renewal date in order to stop the upcoming charge. Once a renewal has processed and the order has entered fulfillment, the 12-hour change window applies to that order just like any new order. For full details, please see our Subscription Management policy and our Returns & Refunds policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_EEJJ9V": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "Can I change my order after I place it?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — within a 12-hour window. After you place your order, you have 12 hours to cancel, change your shipping address, modify your quantity, or adjust your product selection. Email support@hairscriptsbybevy.com with your order number and the change you need.<br/><br/>After 12 hours, your order moves into our fulfillment queue and we can no longer make changes to it. This is a strict cutoff with no exceptions — once your order is picked, packed, and labeled, the address on the label is final. For complete details, please see our Returns & Refunds policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_NyNBNJ": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "What's your shipping policy?",
            "answer": "<p>Free shipping on all subscription orders within the United States. One-time orders ship at standard rates calculated at checkout. Most orders ship within 2–5 business days from the date of order, and you'll receive a tracking number by email once your package is on its way.<br/><br/>Shipping times do not include weekends, federal holidays, or processing time at the fulfillment center. For complete shipping details — including international shipping, address accuracy requirements, and delivery acceptance — please see our Shipping & Delivery policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_6XHyDH": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "Do you ship internationally?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, we ship to select international destinations. International shipping rates are calculated at checkout based on destination and weight, and your order may also be subject to customs duties, taxes, and import fees imposed by your destination country. These additional charges are the responsibility of the recipient.<br/><br/>International packages may be subject to customs review and delays beyond our control. If your country isn't currently available at checkout, please email support@hairscriptsbybevy.com and we'll let you know when we expand to your region. For complete international shipping terms, please see our Shipping & Delivery policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_6P4V78": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "What's your return and refund policy?",
            "answer": "<p>Because HairScripts™ is a consumable supplement product, all sales are final once your order has been processed and shipped. We do not offer refunds on opened, used, or unused product after fulfillment.<br/><br/>The only exceptions: (1) one-time orders cancelled within 12 hours of purchase before fulfillment begins receive a full refund, (2) damaged or defective products are eligible for replacement when reported within 7 days of delivery, and (3) subscription renewals processed due to a verified system error on our end will be refunded or credited within 5 business days.</p><p>Hair growth takes time — most women don't see meaningful results until the 90-day mark. We encourage you to read through our science page, customer testimonials, and ingredient breakdown before purchasing. For complete details, please see our Returns & Refunds policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_TReYFQ": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "What if my package is lost or stolen after delivery?",
            "answer": "<p>If your tracking shows your package as delivered and the carrier has provided proof of delivery (timestamped photo, GPS coordinates, signature, or call attempt), HairScripts™ is not responsible for packages that go missing after that point. The package has legally left our hands and is in the carrier's delivery confirmation.<br/><br/>If you can't locate a package marked as delivered: check your front door, mailroom, building lobby, and with neighbors. Wait 24–48 hours — some carriers mark packages delivered before the actual drop-off. If you still can't find it, you'll need to file a claim directly with the shipping carrier using your tracking number. We're happy to provide the proof of delivery documentation we received from the carrier to support your claim — email support@hairscriptsbybevy.com with your order number.</p><p>For complete details on lost or stolen packages, damaged products, and how to file claims, please see our Returns & Refunds policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_QBbDK7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "What if my package arrives damaged?",
            "answer": "<p>If your bottles arrive physically damaged — broken, leaking, crushed, or otherwise unusable — we'll take care of you. Email support@hairscriptsbybevy.com within 7 days of receiving your package with your order number, clear photos of the damaged bottles, clear photos of the shipping packaging, and a short description of what happened.Once we verify the damage, we'll reship the affected bottles to you at no additional cost and file the carrier claim on our end. Damage claims must be reported within 7 days of delivery — reports submitted after that window are not eligible for replacement, as we cannot file a successful claim with the carrier outside their reporting window.</p>"
          }
        }
